Z||000000||RobertVol||02-03-2000||11:19 PM||||I have an 88 gt with only 52,000 mls on it but recently when you come to a complete stop and then hit the gas and take off the clutch engages with no problem but you can hear something making a noise like a rod or something moving. i dont here after initial take off aand engaging into first gear. also while shifting at this time it "SEEMS" you can feel it in the shifting motion. does not seem to cause a proble with shifting but its bugging the heck out of me!!! any suggestions. (maybe loose shift rod?) ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-03-2000||11:50 PM||||Possible movement under high torque and light shimmy under no load.  Worn or loose mount point somewhere.  Shift link is cable, it might have a 'feel' if it's vibrating.  Those dam&ed gremlins also seem more active after winter solstice.  ||||reg||1
